Outside Connecticut and California, baby bonds programs are limited and early-stage. Vermont's "First Steps Forward" pilot, authorized by the Legislature in 2025 (H.55), is still in its fundraising phase. Its proposed model would invest $3,200 for each Medicaid-born child in Caledonia, Essex, and Orleans counties born July 1, 2027, to June 30, 2030. Those funds could be claimed at ages 18 to 30 for a Vermont home or business, education or job training, or retirement. Other states have bills or frameworks whose status changes as legislatures act, so check your state treasurer's office, which is where Vermont posts [its pilot's current status](https://www.vermonttreasurer.gov/economic-empowerment-division/baby-bonds).